# Check every text file out with LF, on Windows too.
#
# The TypeScript and Swift test suites read the same committed fixtures under
# apps/ios/PhrenKit/Tests/PhrenKitTests/Fixtures/ and compare them byte for
# byte — that shared corpus is the whole proof that both implementations agree
# on the store format. Git's default autocrlf rewrites those bytes on a Windows
# checkout, so the fixtures stopped matching what either implementation writes:
# findings dates parsed as "unknown", and a rendered tasks.md compared LF against
# a CRLF fixture. Store files phren itself writes are LF everywhere as well.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
